# AMD modules

Cognos loads `KDB3/js/**` through its RequireJS. The host does not understand ES modules, so every production file is exactly one AMD module:

```js
define(["../tabs/state/selectors.js"], function (_tabsSelectors) {
  "use strict";

  function readHeaderVisible(_KDB) { return _KDB.state.header.status === "active"; }
  function readHeaderTabId(_KDB) { return _tabsSelectors.readActiveTabId(_KDB); }

  return { readHeaderVisible: readHeaderVisible, readHeaderTabId: readHeaderTabId };
});
```

- Dependency paths are relative and end in `.js`; the array order matches the parameter order.
- A module returns one value: a function, a factory, or an object of **related** named exports (`selectors.js`, `state.js`, `config.js`, a kit file). Not a grab bag of unrelated functions.
- Declare helpers as named function declarations at factory scope. Short inline callbacks (`map`, `filter`, listeners that call one function) are fine. A controller factory defines its API methods as closures inside the factory (see the `index.js` skeleton in `feature-structure.mdc`); do not nest further function definitions inside those methods.
- Start async work in a named function that takes `_KDB`, its arguments and an `AbortSignal`; no inline `async` IIFEs inside methods.
- Runtime dependencies (`_KDB`, services, facets) are passed in by the registering code or read from `_KDB` namespaces; code dependencies come through AMD imports. Deep files never use `window._KDB` or `window.top.getKDB()`.
- Many imports in one file are a hint that it holds more than one concept; there is no fixed limit.

## Forbidden in `KDB3/js/**`

- `import` / `export`, CommonJS `require(...)`, the simplified `define(function (require, exports, module) {...})` wrapper.
- More than one `define` per file; conditional or dynamic `define`.
- Side effects at file top level outside `define`; module-level mutable state that outlives one `_KDB` instance (per-instance state lives in the controller closure, `_KDB.state` or `_KDB.runtime`).

## Outside `KDB3/js`

`tools/` (repo root) is Node ESM (`.mjs`, no npm dependencies). Tools load production files through an AMD shim, never through ES `import`, and production code never imports from `tools/`.
